PARITY ARITHMETIC (reproduced VERBATIM from the web source — cross-platform value parity,
NOT a "corrected" version; the source's miles-as-metres quirk is preserved on purpose)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  energyKwh   = convertEnergyFromSI(total_energy_added_wh, 'kWh')            = wh / 1000
  totalKwh    = Σ energyKwh
  totalCost   = Σ (session.cost ?? energyKwh * costPerKwh)
  distanceMi  = totalKwh * 3.5                                              (AVG_MI_PER_KWH)
  costPerDist = costPerDistanceUnit(totalKwh, distanceMi)  where the fn treats its 2nd arg as SI
                metres: cost = totalKwh*costPerKwh ; distance = convertDistanceFromSI(distanceMi,
                unitPref) [ /1000 km · /1609.344 mi · /0.3048 ft ] ; return distance>0 ? cost/distance : nil
  gasCost     = estimateGasCost(distanceMi)  -> distanceMi2 = convertDistanceFromSI(distanceMi,'mi') ;
                gallons = distanceMi2 / mpg ; liter? gallons*3.78541*price : gallons*price ; (mpg/price>0)
  gasSavings  = gasCost==nil ? nil : gasCost - totalCost
  fmtNumber   = en_US grouped, fixed fraction digits, half-away-from-zero ; formatCurrency =
                currencySymbol + fmtNumber(amount, precision). compact = formatCurrency(totalCost, 0).
  Ground truth cross-checked in Node against the literal web fns, then pinned + re-verified by an
  executed Swift host harness AND the on-simulator XCTest suite (identical strings on all three):
    mi+gas:  "100.0 kWh" · "3 sessions" · "$13.50" · "$0.12/kWh" · costPerDist=55.177508571.. -> "$55.178"
             · gasSavings=-13.47462734.. -> "$-13.47" · compact "$14" · footer "Saved $-13.47 vs gas"
    km+litre: "$34.286" · "$-13.45"          no-gas/EUR: "€15" · "€68.972" · savings "—" + "Set gas price…"

